{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>And six years you shall sow your land.</b> It would have been fitting to say 'thus shall you do to your vineyards and olive groves,' and it mentions the entire language in the second person. So too we find regarding the Sabbath that the language is in the second person: 'you shall do your work, your ox and your donkey, the son of your maidservant and the stranger' — the Sabbath and the sabbatical year are equal in this respect, something you will not find in the Jubilee, for there the language is not in the second person but in the third person, as it is written (Leviticus 25:11): 'you shall not sow and you shall not reap its aftergrowth and you shall not harvest its untrimmed vines.' Now this is the reason for the matter: the Sabbath and the sabbatical year, after the Sabbath passes, he is destined to return to his work at the conclusion of the Sabbath, and so too with the sabbatical year, after the seventh year passes — in which cultivation of the land is forbidden — he is destined to return to cultivation at the conclusion of the seventh year; therefore it says 'your field and your vineyard and your olive grove,' in the manner of what is yours. But in the Jubilee, which is holy, when all labors cease and everything is sabbath and rest and labor does not follow it, the language is in the third person, as it says 'its aftergrowth,' to indicate that to YHWH is the land and its fullness, and you have nothing in it. And the language itself likewise indicates, for here in the sabbatical year it mentions 'you shall let it rest and abandon it,' meaning that we are obligated to let it lie fallow, but it is not released from us, for we are destined to return to cultivation of the land after the sabbatical year — unlike the Jubilee, in which it is released from us, and one returns to what is his, the ancestral holding of the land. And this is explained here."], :book :exodus, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 23, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:03:18.549682774Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}